:R-HSA-8939247  a           obo:GO_0001959 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "The RUNX1:CBFB complex regulates transcription of at least a couple of genes involved in interleukin signaling. The LIFR gene, a direct transcriptional target of the RUNX1:CBFB complex (Qadi et al. 2016), encodes the receptor for the leukemia inhibitory factor (LIF), a member of the interleukin-6 family. LIFR is implicated in hematopoiesis, embryo implantation, placental formation and nervous system development (Nicola et al. 2015). In association with its co-activator ELF1, the RUNX1:CBFB complex stimulates transcription of the IL3 gene, encoding interleukin-3 (Mao et al. 1999)." ;
        rdfs:label          "RUNX1 regulates transcription of genes involved in interleukin signaling" ;
        dc:contributor      "Reviewed: Chuang, Linda Shyue Huey, 2016-12-20" , "Edited: Orlic-Milacic, Marija, 2017-05-09" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Reviewed: Ito, Yoshiaki, 2016-12-20" , "Authored: Orlic-Milacic, Marija, 2016-09-14" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-8939247" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-8878171/R-HSA-8878171> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

